* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-lock-detector-window (issue #38, Part of #16)
* Single-device DC extraction: lock_detector.XRPU (rhigh, w=0.5u l=6u), the
* same instance parameters as ../netlist-snapshots/lock_detector.spice's XRPU
* line. Forces 1 uA through the resistor and reads V(N1)/I to get R at the
* resistor corner + temperature this run.sh instantiation substitutes below.
*
* Why this record needs the resistor value as its OWN measurement rather than
* only as an implicit part of the block transient: XRPU and XCW together are
* the integrating node's time constant, and whether that time constant is
* long or short compared with one reference period is the single fact that
* decides whether this block is an integrator (a lock detector) or a
* combinational pass-through of `WIDE` (a chatter generator). The block
* transient shows the *consequence*; this deck plus tb_extract_c.sp.tmpl give
* the R and C that *cause* it, so ../records/RECORD-001 can state the
* mechanism rather than infer it.
*
* Unlike the `cp` DUT (all-MOS, no resistor -- see
* ../../sg13cmos5l-cp-icp-trim/), this DUT genuinely has a resistor-corner
* axis: cornerRES.lib's own rsh_rhigh is 1020 / 1360 / 1700 ohm/sq at
* res_bcs / res_typ / res_wcs, a +/-25% spread that lands directly on the
* integrating node's time constant.
*
* Template placeholders (substituted by ../testbench/run.sh, not meant to be
* run directly): @RES_CORNER@ (res_typ|res_bcs|res_wcs, cornerRES.lib),
* @TEMP@ (degC), @W@, @L@ (device geometry).

.lib $PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @RES_CORNER@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@

Xrpu n1 0 sub! rhigh w=@W@ l=@L@ m=1 b=0
Vsub sub! 0 0
I1 n1 0 dc 1u

.control
op
let rval = abs(v(n1)/1e-6)
print rval
.endc
.end
